WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.410
ALEXIS MOUSSINE-POUCHKINE:
If you've seen previous GCP

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.210
Essentials videos,
you should now

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:06.250
have a good sense of
what GCP has to offer.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.330
It's time to get your feet
wet and your hands dirty.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.640
And if you haven't, then
consider checking out

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.970
the series playlist.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.250
In this video, we'll
talk about all the ways

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:21.050
you can experience GCP with
hands-on code labs, tutorials,

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:25.490
online courses, and solutions,
all at little or no cost.

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:28.328
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:34.620
Before we talk about
hands-on resources,

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.070
let me remind you about
the Google Cloud home

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.490
page at cloud.google.com.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.440
It all starts there.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.740
Product documentation
lives there, for instance.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:48.440
And chances are you will
spend some quality time there

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:53.220
as you learn and research
specific products and APIs.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:56.540
Make sure you check out the
Documentation Quick Start.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:00.410
These 30-minute tutorials offer
a step-by-step walk-through

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:04.680
of some basic tasks, such
as creating a Linux VM,

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.580
storing a file and sharing it,
deploying a Docker container

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:12.480
image, running a label
detection on a photograph,

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.176
or deploying an
application on App Engine.

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:19.870
You can also find interactive
tutorials embedded right

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:21.470
into the console.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.460
Select one of the dozen
or so product tutorials

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:27.670
and let the tutorial
guide you step-by-step

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:31.740
through the console
user interface.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.980
If you're looking for
self-based hands-on experience,

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.490
we have a lot in store for you.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:43.880
First, Google code labs are
available at g.co/codelabs,

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.790
and they have a very
rich cloud section.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:49.040
There are more
than 200 free labs,

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.440
covering the vast
majority of GCP products.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.410
You can sort by category,
duration, and publish dates.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:01.190
Each lab should only
cost you $1 or $2,

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:04.700
which can be covered by the
$300 free trial credits.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:08.030
But do make sure to follow the
CodeLab's clean-up instructions

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:12.180
to properly delete all
resources that can incur costs.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.320
Second, there is Qwiklabs.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.760
If you're planning
for a certification

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:20.300
or would like to take a series
of related hands-on labs,

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.910
also known as
Quests, then Qwiklabs

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:25.400
offers you a
personalized platform

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.740
to track your progress.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:31.370
Simply sign up for a free
account, buy some credits,

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.570
and start a quest.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:36.810
Each lab comes with a
real, but temporary, GCP

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:40.470
account and a project ID
available for the duration

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.780
of the lab.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:45.190
Note, also, that Qwiklabs
is the hands-on tool

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:49.960
that Coursera uses to deliver
its courses and specialization.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.990
Now, getting your hands
on individual products

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:56.380
and understanding the scope
and features is great,

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:00.040
but understanding how different
products actually work together

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.630
is also very useful.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.640
And this is where
Solutions come into play.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.000
These detailed,
technical articles

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.070
often come with
source code and are

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:13.120
grouped into categories, such
as modernize infrastructure,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.350
migrate workloads, hybrid
cloud, HPC, big data analytics,

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:21.550
machine learning, IoT,
continuous delivery,

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.680
serverless API
management, et cetera.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.950
You can also browse by
industry or vertical solutions,

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:33.140
such as retail, energy,
financial services, gaming,

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:34.850
and others.

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:38.720
These solutions are all based
on customer best practices

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.510
and common use cases.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:43.610
And they come with detailed
descriptions and code

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.860
to make sure you can
learn from others

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:49.000
and jump-start your
GCP developments.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.060
As you can see, there's
plenty of hands-on material

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:54.600
that is available
and waiting for you.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.780
So what are you waiting for?

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:59.410
Grab a tutorial, take a
code lab, study a solution,

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.510
and get those hands dirty.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.660
If you like this video, please
like, subscribe, comment,

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:08.260
share, and look forward to
more GCP Essentials videos.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.310
[MUSIC PLAYING]

